1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,375
Hi. I am Anton.

2
00:00:01,655 --> 00:00:06,836
I work rotational shifts at an oil field, two weeks away from home at a time.

3
00:00:07,116 --> 00:00:13,040
On my rotations off, I build verification infrastructure for the physical world, on Solana.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,182
Every number that reaches a market starts as a claim somebody typed.

5
00:00:19,462 --> 00:00:23,287
A spreadsheet cell can be edited. A portal can be inflated.

6
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:26,333
And the same megawatt-hour can be sold twice.

7
00:00:26,613 --> 00:00:31,875
Markets move in milliseconds, while verification still runs on annual audits.

8
00:00:32,155 --> 00:00:34,863
The result has a name: greenwashing.

9
00:00:35,613 --> 00:00:41,502
Axis Protocol closes that gap: identity, proof, attestation, policy.

10
00:00:41,782 --> 00:00:53,348
On the device, an Ed25519 key inside an NXP SE050 secure element signs every reading — the device itself is the signature.

11
00:00:53,628 --> 00:00:58,042
Then at least two staked oracles vote on the same canonical hash.

12
00:00:58,322 --> 00:01:03,723
A contradictory vote is a slashing event, and minting waits for a finalised attestation.

13
00:01:04,004 --> 00:01:07,106
One compromised oracle cannot create value.

14
00:01:07,856 --> 00:01:10,808
Fifty-eight on-chain instructions in Rust.

15
00:01:11,088 --> 00:01:16,594
Two hundred and seventy-two tests pass: Rust, Node, Python and Foundry.

16
00:01:16,873 --> 00:01:23,865
The full stack is live on devnet today — ESP32 firmware, secure element, two independent oracles.

17
00:01:24,145 --> 00:01:30,231
A finalised attestation, and a mint that only executed because the gate said required equals true.

18
00:01:30,511 --> 00:01:33,927
Every proof and mint is public — verify it yourself.

19
00:01:34,677 --> 00:01:38,560
Why me? I have no degree, no team and no funding.

20
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:46,252
Four months of nights and rotations off. I wrote the firmware, the contracts, the oracles and the AI layer myself.

21
00:01:46,532 --> 00:01:49,867
I got tired of watching physical data be trusted on faith.

22
00:01:50,147 --> 00:01:57,434
This is not a sprint for me. It is a mission: make the physical world provable. Judge me by the code, not by the pitch.

23
00:01:59,677 --> 00:02:07,983
So here is my ask. I need one real pilot: a solar site, a meter, an operator — anyone whose data should be provable.

24
00:02:08,263 --> 00:02:11,888
And I need mentors who have taken infrastructure like this to mainnet.

25
00:02:12,168 --> 00:02:16,757
The protocol is open, the devnet is live, and the code is public.

26
00:02:17,037 --> 00:02:19,211
If that is you, let us talk.

27
00:02:19,961 --> 00:02:23,561
ENRG — verification infrastructure for the physical world. github.com/AntonGrid/ENRG
